#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287983 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bb4f677-6e20-5d48-8adf-dad8e569076e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1,y=8$ and $z=-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285033} {:answer/id #uuid "67b6832b-f7f1-55d1-92dd-f7c48ee15a21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1,y=4$ and $z=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285735} {:answer/id #uuid "9b6c5f1f-a44d-56e0-b1b5-4ebcaafd017f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1,y=6$ and $z=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286213} {:answer/id #uuid "9e0477fe-23d0-5b2c-af42-8e02c492ff15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1,y=2$ and $z=3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286234} {:answer/id #uuid "bcba1021-c3fa-5be5-90b6-ccdceb2d3943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1,y=5$ and $z=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e0477fe-23d0-5b2c-af42-8e02c492ff15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1,y=2$ and $z=3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286234} :answer-field/id #uuid "13c51648-1907-5520-9df6-2d1f4963b562" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287184}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "76260352-1678-5f91-b36f-3214c8df1e0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-20263" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z &=6 \\\\ y+z &=5 \\\\ 2x+3y+2z &=14\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and hence solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2 & 14\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2 & 14\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :=-{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z &=6 \\\\ y+z &=5 \\\\ z &=3,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=3$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+(3)=5\\,⟹\\,y=5-3=2.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=2$ and $z=3$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(2)+(3)=6\\,⟹\\,x=6-5=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=1,y=2$ and $z=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287997 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15719692-f572-52e2-92ef-7c37695a20ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284977} {:answer/id #uuid "8eb9ba6d-8ad5-5004-96ed-80c84894925e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286091} {:answer/id #uuid "bc5c7bb0-6725-548b-b664-64d4ff92c96b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286504} {:answer/id #uuid "d6bbdd67-60e8-56e1-96f6-8012386dd066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286742} {:answer/id #uuid "f2e5b59d-43dc-5f6c-8987-626af7040c4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287014}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc5c7bb0-6725-548b-b664-64d4ff92c96b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286504} :answer-field/id #uuid "28841267-b70d-52db-841b-c4f0d84407a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287232}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e202a5f2-1485-54d2-ad75-6c42b9340de9" :question/math-academy-id "q-20524" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 6 & 21\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 6 & 21\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287998 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17efca8f-87be-5b95-8922-289fdb1d26ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285001} {:answer/id #uuid "3c4254ad-d231-50fd-9b68-9ebbd2ce5ce4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285352} {:answer/id #uuid "45a723dd-0ef1-5ec0-b478-73144022c495" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285424} {:answer/id #uuid "75525907-933a-53d6-ae44-4d6d45f4ca9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285870} {:answer/id #uuid "ccf19ccd-17f1-5cf4-8f69-4973c62ab6fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c4254ad-d231-50fd-9b68-9ebbd2ce5ce4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285352} :answer-field/id #uuid "51bb4809-5d86-5a66-b4a7-5e6d674e0405" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287329}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a9aba0f5-8a1c-5403-81c5-fd64e80722c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-20533" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+2z &=0 \\\\ y+2z &=0 \\\\ x+y+3z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287999 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09ae6737-5709-5299-9355-f610cf32cf10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-11,y=4$ and $z=4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284870} {:answer/id #uuid "38432a32-b421-5cb9-b804-edecfba79df6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-1,y=4$ and $z=-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285312} {:answer/id #uuid "b532826d-782c-5acc-b69d-27c5cf349663" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=13,y=-4$ and $z=-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286436} {:answer/id #uuid "ddb9a50d-a3e7-56d7-b7e0-47332e68cf82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-2,y=4$ and $z=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286806} {:answer/id #uuid "f110becd-084a-5b17-b76a-616cfd4c91b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=4,y=5$ and $z=-6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f110becd-084a-5b17-b76a-616cfd4c91b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=4,y=5$ and $z=-6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286999} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b2ad410-5feb-53d6-a57d-187523cf9154" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287438}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "00b50258-32a4-58d0-8a62-9857f481b38c" :question/math-academy-id "q-20542" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+2z &=-3 \\\\ x+2y+2z &=2 \\\\ 3x+4y+4z &=8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and hence solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 4 & 8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 4 & 8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 4 & 8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 17\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -6\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+2z &=-3 \\\\ y &=5 \\\\ z &=-6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. Substituting both $y=5$ and $z=-6$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+5+2(-6)=-3\\,⟹\\,x-7=-3\\,⟹\\,x=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=4,$ $y=5,$ and $z=-6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288008 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c247114-0265-5d19-950c-d6ddadbc52e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3-2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284888} {:answer/id #uuid "290d4310-b38e-58a7-b7f8-229614a89956" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3+2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285148} {:answer/id #uuid "2bad0c5b-8898-5e4a-8e57-39537797a08c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3+2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285168} {:answer/id #uuid "606e281f-cd18-58f3-89f3-488a6defa97e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2+3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285672} {:answer/id #uuid "e873edde-7317-52df-9cf0-cc4cec745284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3-2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286914}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2bad0c5b-8898-5e4a-8e57-39537797a08c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3+2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285168} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9e4910b-9053-5d68-9d88-04077e065b78" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287630}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "64e30738-40d0-5a54-8cdd-1cc83ec4b628" :question/math-academy-id "q-20782" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -7 & 14 & 21\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -7 & 14 & 21\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=-3 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-2y=-3.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-3+2y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-3+2y \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3+2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288009 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47c97c9a-b257-58e1-b8f0-fedf81973715" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2+4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285449} {:answer/id #uuid "6572eab8-0051-57e0-9e01-2a886e1ff7f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2-4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285709} {:answer/id #uuid "7fb0f231-ef58-570a-a217-3ac725a9c673" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1+4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285962} {:answer/id #uuid "a610291f-fe71-59f4-ba82-34c306fd05eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286302} {:answer/id #uuid "df55ab77-72af-5c93-956c-d075379dc2c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2+4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286824}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6572eab8-0051-57e0-9e01-2a886e1ff7f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2-4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285709} :answer-field/id #uuid "613521d7-e573-530c-9e5e-83c95de64ea2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287354}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e9e4d803-6c25-5024-8fca-536e9832cf45" :question/math-academy-id "q-20783" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+4y &=2 \\\\ 2x+8y &=4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+4y &=2 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+4y=2.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=2-4y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2-4y \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2-4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288020 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15f1cb44-5b06-5d4d-9607-9ad3cbf2af14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1-3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284985} {:answer/id #uuid "6d6fcd9a-23a6-5453-9d08-4d210d1b7d8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}7+3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285795} {:answer/id #uuid "7c25a4a3-f7cb-549a-ae3e-01af8eacb8bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5+3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285932} {:answer/id #uuid "9d5c5078-f3f5-5c82-bd8d-335557d74371" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-7-3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286228} {:answer/id #uuid "ec9ee132-1b40-541a-bae6-15241f57f92e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}7-3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286955}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d6fcd9a-23a6-5453-9d08-4d210d1b7d8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}7+3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285795} :answer-field/id #uuid "53d20d8e-decf-56db-bd2e-b51650f71249" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287334}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "25615c72-6956-5e2b-84cd-a6850d4c806d" :question/math-academy-id "q-20958" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 28\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 28\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=7 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-3y=7.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=7+3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=7+3y \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}7+3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288021 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d711321-0fdb-5d3b-bfac-97034f5be8f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285052} {:answer/id #uuid "7f073f29-e6f4-56ac-901f-2e8a7b8dc9f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5-3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285958} {:answer/id #uuid "86c5daa8-b3b8-5758-9b80-3a426311e501" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5-3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286024} {:answer/id #uuid "9ff0d8ee-a71c-5f88-81f8-7328e1c2febc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5-4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286245} {:answer/id #uuid "c5c46c80-ae3f-508f-aaba-0e3f84db3710" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5-4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286603}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ff0d8ee-a71c-5f88-81f8-7328e1c2febc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5-4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286245} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d2d960c-2fb5-52ad-a79f-06087dbf3f48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287211}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6b84d9fd-d3bf-5ad1-8468-147cba84321e" :question/math-academy-id "q-20960" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}8x+32y &=-40 \\\\ 5x+20y &=-25.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}8 & 32 & -40 \\\\ 5 & 20 & -25\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}8 & 32 & -40 \\\\ 5 & 20 & -25\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 20 & -25\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+4y &=-5 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+4y=-5.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-5-4y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-5-4y \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5-4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292861 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35a277db-ec1d-5339-9e82-45fd36df7e02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290850}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35a277db-ec1d-5339-9e82-45fd36df7e02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290850} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d3641ea-9f18-5805-b931-3c38516383e8" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292070} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c39433f4-5fcd-59f3-ba21-01b309286853" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291472}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c39433f4-5fcd-59f3-ba21-01b309286853" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291472} :answer-field/id #uuid "c16a15af-7e49-5cb5-9440-b33b17b184d3" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292329} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b88eef00-3a55-54c1-b21e-9b6cb90f1cbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b88eef00-3a55-54c1-b21e-9b6cb90f1cbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291433} :answer-field/id #uuid "e108afa3-c6ec-50a1-9832-368f277dc1cf" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292436} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4c98fa9-6904-5e37-89ee-6d96692b12ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4c98fa9-6904-5e37-89ee-6d96692b12ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291352} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4e11e98-00f4-5945-bb4e-c6d309dda5cd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292450}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9f215cc9-2733-5448-8e6a-2bb133106105" :question/math-academy-id "q-275522" :question/problem "Calculate the product $D{I}_{2}$ given that ${I}_{2}$ is the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix and\n$$\n\\displaystyle D=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$D\\cdot I_2=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>{{field-4}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Any matrix, when multiplied by an identity matrix, remains unchanged (assuming that the multiplication is well defined).\n\nThe matrix $D$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and ${I}_{2}$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix too. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication is well defined and \n\n$$\nD\\cdot {I}_{2}=D=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292862 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ba8f9b9-ebe4-5a92-ad85-2a5904c716b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291226}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ba8f9b9-ebe4-5a92-ad85-2a5904c716b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291226} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c71c1d5-29c4-5775-add9-5e009062a4d6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292231} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e10b6b5-317f-5bfd-9061-ca77b2bc0961" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e10b6b5-317f-5bfd-9061-ca77b2bc0961" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290889} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc3870f6-6b6d-59e8-8173-92df64daaeb3" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292314} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4898d33f-f280-50da-be31-36b295222808" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4898d33f-f280-50da-be31-36b295222808" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290931} :answer-field/id #uuid "d71ef47c-19b6-5afb-8eb0-dcde40324c55" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292389}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "18c8e800-9586-55d4-91d2-1e71b341e0e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-275527" :question/problem "Find the product $AB,$ if\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5} & -5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & \\sqrt{5} & -6 \\\\ 7 & -8 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand \n$$\n\\displaystyle B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$AB=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-3}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $B$ is the $2$nd *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ by the $2$nd *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3},$ the result must be the $2$nd *column* of $A.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5} & -5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & \\sqrt{5} & -6 \\\\ 7 & -8 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5}\\cdot 0+(-5)\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 0 \\\\ 3\\cdot 0+\\sqrt{5}\\cdot 1+(-6)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 7\\cdot 0+(-8)\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302051 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bc404a6-d316-58c1-b56c-a595600e5fdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299992} {:answer/id #uuid "4f27f1d5-de6e-5780-b1ae-07308f92edd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300375} {:answer/id #uuid "7bb1b90c-e720-592f-8ba9-f2f4f1bd0389" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300577} {:answer/id #uuid "85d6c1f1-b43e-5c0a-925c-0e868e7f0b14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300634} {:answer/id #uuid "e2cac16f-758b-5dd9-b61a-f47b814cb964" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301088}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2cac16f-758b-5dd9-b61a-f47b814cb964" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301088} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e346c9e-f73f-5c61-a8d0-3c774b70c08c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301429}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f41cbfea-5742-50ae-9cb7-b244cecfac9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-32133" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302068 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46f3e548-ea7a-5436-bed5-5b7a9a6026d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300320} {:answer/id #uuid "4ad8d28c-e868-5868-8413-6322f84a2fe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300347} {:answer/id #uuid "7e0c5047-959e-5134-8822-7384bc80845a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300586} {:answer/id #uuid "cc271c4a-91a0-5cce-b573-018619a7dc65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{3}{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300982} {:answer/id #uuid "f7517fe5-d015-57e3-a049-a5efb53cec23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301181}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e0c5047-959e-5134-8822-7384bc80845a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300586} :answer-field/id #uuid "918cd991-3826-55e2-a035-fd8fa5f520dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301691}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "90efc42e-c582-5ebf-b710-fc84d57b2391" :question/math-academy-id "q-32144" :question/problem "Suppose that the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}:=-\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{3}$ is applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:=-\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{3}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302070 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35469338-35ab-59b2-8e2e-76d36fdf8640" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300224} {:answer/id #uuid "54871df1-41e8-5ee2-8d57-eff6a18da986" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 &